### An observation that belongs to 19.3, recorded now so it is not reinvented

Two arms so far (q36 and q37, one per condition) **appended the three-step `PROTOCOL_CHECK`
directive block to `CLAUDE.md` themselves**, noting that §1 branches on the sentinel alone and
would otherwise have called it a noop.

19.3 measured Write Gate coverage at **55%** in trees where that block was **absent** from the
file the tool actually loads, and the gate lived only in `00-ai-rules.md`. If an agent installs
the block when Step 0's §5 gets a chance to run, 19.3's 55% is a **floor and not a ceiling**, and
the two conditions are not comparable. Not treated as a result here, and not folded into 19.3 —
it is a new question with a cheap round behind it.

